From 3fc9f85e03fe0340310f46f0a3a297b6be868b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:19:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] button prompts: device icons over texture-pack images too,
 drawn at the internal resolution

A pack image replacing a texture of buttons/map.json kept its PlayStation
icons. gs_buttonmatch.h finds the icons in the pack image with the original
texture's icon pixels as templates (translations move them: tutorial and
message-box pictures), only confident matches, never covering text;
gs_buttonpack.h covers each with the colour around it and draws the style's
icon. Icons (map spots, pack images, text placeholders) are composed at
ga2_hitext::iconScale(): the sharp-text scale, at least 4x
(GA2_ICON_SCALE overrides). Tests: ga2_buttonmatch_tests.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
